          "filename": "Passage of Humaitá.jpg",
          "caption": "A watercolour by retired Brazilian admiral Trajano Augusto de Carvalho depicting a scene from the Passage of Humaitá, 19 February 1868.  Shellbursts illuminate the night sky revealing Brazilan ironclads dashing past the Paraguayan fortress of Humaitá or waiting their turn to do so.  Carvalho claimed to have researched his historical paintings carefully and the ships' outlines and the topography of the fortress on the River Paraguay are generally correct, although in the placement of vessels he has allowed himself some artistic licence.",
